@*
    My Audits (migration 555, 2026-11-14, sir) -- Phase 3 of the audit flow
    redesign (docs/audit-flow-redesign.md).

    Screen key : `org-my-audits`
    Group      : Audit Assurance
    Menu       : nav-assurance -> My Audits (555, display order 468)
    Backend    :
        POST /practice/api/org-assurance/my-audits/prepare
        GET  /practice/api/org-assurance/my-audits
        GET  /practice/api/org-assurance/executions/{id}/live-scope?organizationId=
        GET  /practice/api/org-assurance/executions/{id}/scope-exclusions?organizationId=
        GET  /practice/api/org-assurance/executions/{id}/continuous-assurance?organizationId=
        (567: the 558 responses endpoints are no longer called here --
        Working Papers opens the Workpapers page)
        POST /practice/api/org-assurance/executions/{id}/freeze-scope
        GET  /practice/api/org-assurance/executions/{id}/scope-review?organizationId=   (563)
    The caller is the session employee (the Web tier stamps it); the list
    shows only engagements where that employee is the Assigned Auditor.

    FLOW (sir's decisions):
      * Opening the page starts the engagements that are due (From <=
        today): one execution per audit, scope LIVE.
      * Review & Freeze Scope: the live scope (the audit's scope now,
        narrowed to the engagement's Branch). Untick what does not apply --
        each exclusion needs a reason. Freeze is FINAL and starts the audit
        (Planned -> In Progress).
      * View Scope: a frozen scope and its exclusions, read-only.
      * 563 (2026-11-15, sir) -- Scope Builder Step 3, Review and Confirm
        (Audit Change spec 4.2.1, phase C2), in the same frame under the
        scope list: "Related GRAC Intelligence" -- Step 2's discovery over
        THIS engagement's practice instances (the scope list's "Why in
        scope" column comes from it too). Per category an Include tick
        (Practice Instances are the scope list itself); open a category
        (child row, as Step 2) to untick a record -- with a reason -- or
        add a manual item; Search filters the records. Freeze sends the
        review with the exclusions and keeps it as the approved scope
        snapshot (version 1); View Scope shows that snapshot read-only.
      * Continuous Assurance (556, Phase 4): over the scope (frozen, or live
        now) -- each scope item -> its practice instances (direct, or
        through the Operationalize resolution) -> their Execution /
        Assurance obligations -> implementation status and last task.
        Summary counts each obligation once. Read-only, same frame.
      * Working Papers (567, replaces 558's Answer Questions): opens the
        Workpapers page on the execution (the id in the navigation code,
        gracSecureNav) -- working papers per question, review, conclusion,
        findings raised by the auditor (nothing automatic).
      * No popups (sir, 543 rule): each opens in a CHILD ROW under the
        audit's row -- the Audit Plans child row (sir, 2026-11-14: "like the
        child row"): .oa-pl-wrap list, tr.oa-pl-items-row > td > .oa-pl-items
        (44px indent, accent down the left edge with the open row
        .oa-pl-open, inner grids not height-capped). Inside it the frame
        keeps the Audit Configuration caption / save bar (.oa-cfg-frame,
        .oa-cfg-savebar -- the section carries .oa-cfg for those). One open
        at a time.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>@Model.Description</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel oa-cfg" id="oaMyRoot">
    <div class="pm-toolbar" style="flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
        <select id="oaMyFilterState" aria-label="State">
            <option value="">All audits</option>
            <option value="ScopeLive">Scope to freeze</option>
            <option value="InProgress">In progress</option>
            <option value="Upcoming">Upcoming</option>
            <option value="Ready">Not started</option>
            <option value="Done">Done</option>
            <option value="Cancelled">Cancelled</option>
        </select>
        <input id="oaMySearch" type="text" placeholder="Search engagement / audit / branch..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaMyRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-message" id="oaMyMessage" style="display:none; margin-top:10px;"></div>

    <div class="pm-table-wrap oa-pl-wrap" style="margin-top:12px;">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Engagement</th>
                    <th>Audit</th>
                    <th>Branch</th>
                    <th>Scheduled</th>
                    <th>Status</th>
                    <th>Scope</th>
                    <th style="width:70px;"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="oaMyBody">
                <tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Loading your audits...</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

@* ---------- Review & Freeze Scope / View Scope ----------
   The frame waits here and opens in a row under the audit's row
   (Audit Configuration's step frame, 543). *@
<div id="oaMyHolder" hidden>
    <div class="oa-cfg-frame" id="oaMyFrame">
        <p class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaMyFrameCaption"></p>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaMyScopeMessage" style="display:none; margin-bottom:10px;"></div>
        <div id="oaMyScopePane">
            <div class="oa-pl-scope-summary" id="oaMyScopeSummary"></div>
            <div class="pm-table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width:70px;" id="oaMyScopeKeepHead">Keep</th>
                            <th>Type</th>
                            <th>Code</th>
                            <th>Name</th>
                            <th>Why in scope</th>
                            <th id="oaMyScopeReasonHead">Reason for excluding</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="oaMyScopeBody"></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            @* 563: Step 3 Review and Confirm -- the related records, the
               Step 2 category list (Include, child row per category). *@
            <div id="oaMyReview" hidden style="margin-top:16px;">
                <div class="oa-ws-section-head"><h2>Related GRAC Intelligence</h2></div>
                <p class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaMyReviewHint"></p>
                <div class="pm-toolbar" style="flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
                    <input id="oaMyReviewSearch" type="text" placeholder="Search related records..." />
                </div>
                <div class="pm-table-wrap oa-pl-wrap" style="margin-top:8px;">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th style="width:90px;">Include</th>
                                <th>Category</th>
                                <th style="text-align:right; width:110px;">Records</th>
                                <th style="width:60px;"></th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody id="oaMyReviewBody"></tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        @* 556: Continuous Assurance -- same frame, read-only. *@
        <div id="oaMyCaPane" hidden>
            <div class="oa-pl-scope-summary" id="oaMyCaSummary"></div>
            <div class="pm-table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Scope item</th>
                            <th>Practice instance</th>
                            <th>Obligation</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                            <th>Last task</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="oaMyCaBody"></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="oa-flow-nav oa-cfg-savebar">
            <span class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaMyFrameHint"></span>
            <span style="display:flex; gap:8px;">
                <button type="button" id="oaMyScopeCancel" class="pm-button">Close</button>
                <button type="button" id="oaMyScopeFreeze" class="pm-button primary">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i> Freeze Scope
                </button>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="~/js/Shared/secure-nav.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';
    const wf = window.__wfCommon;
    if (!wf) { console.error('__wfCommon missing'); return; }

    const API = '/practice/api/org-assurance';
    const U   = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;

    const STATE_LABEL = {
        Upcoming  : 'Upcoming',
        Ready     : 'Not started',
        ScopeLive : 'Scope to freeze',
        InProgress: 'In progress',
        Done      : 'Done',
        Cancelled : 'Cancelled'
    };

    const state = {
        rows   : [],
        byKey  : {},
        filter : '',
        search : '',
        scope  : { row: null, key: null, items: [], frozen: false }
    };
    let openMenuEl = null, openMenuTrigger = null;

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') boot();
    let booted = false;

    async function boot() {
        if (booted) return; booted = true;
        document.getElementById('oaMyFilterState').addEventListener('change', function (e) { state.filter = e.target.value; render(); });
        document.getElementById('oaMySearch').addEventListener('input', function (e) { state.search = e.target.value.trim().toLowerCase(); render(); });
        document.getElementById('oaMyRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', function () { load(true); });
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeCancel').addEventListener('click', closeScope);
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze').addEventListener('click', freeze);
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeBody').addEventListener('change', onKeepChange);
        wireReview();   // 563
        wireRowMenus();
        await load(true);
    }

    // Opening (and Refresh) starts the engagements that are due, then lists.
    async function load(prepare) {
        wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', '');
        if (prepare) {
            try {
                const r = await fetch(U(API + '/my-audits/prepare'), {
                    method: 'POST', credentials: 'same-origin',
                    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: '{}'
                });
                const j = await safeJson(r);
                if (!r.ok) { showList([], (j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status)); return; }
                const res = (j && (j.data || j.Data)) || [];
                const started = res.filter(function (x) { return x.started ?? x.Started; });
                const failed  = res.filter(function (x) { return !(x.started ?? x.Started); });
                if (failed.length)
                    wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', 'Could not start: ' + failed.map(function (x) {
                        return (x.engagementCode || x.EngagementCode || '') + ' -- ' + (x.message || x.Message || '');
                    }).join('; '), 'error');
                else if (started.length)
                    wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', started.length + ' engagement(s) are due and were started. Review and freeze their scope to begin.', 'ok');
            } catch (err) { wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', 'Could not start the due audits: ' + (err.message || err), 'error'); }
        }
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/my-audits'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) { showList([], (j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status)); return; }
            showList((j && (j.data || j.Data)) || [], null);
        } catch (err) { showList([], err.message || String(err)); }
    }

    function showList(rows, error) {
        state.rows = rows;
        state.byKey = {};
        rows.forEach(function (r, i) { state.byKey[String(i)] = r; });
        if (error) {
            document.getElementById('oaMyBody').innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">' + wf.escape(error) + '</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        render();
    }

    function v(row, camel, pascal) { return row[camel] ?? row[pascal]; }

    function render() {
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyBody');
        const rows = state.rows.map(function (r, i) { return { i: i, r: r }; }).filter(function (x) {
            const r = x.r;
            if (state.filter && v(r, 'auditState', 'AuditState') !== state.filter) return false;
            if (!state.search) return true;
            const hay = [v(r, 'engagementCode', 'EngagementCode'), v(r, 'engagementName', 'EngagementName'),
                         v(r, 'definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode'), v(r, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName'),
                         v(r, 'branchName', 'BranchName'), v(r, 'planName', 'PlanName')].join(' ').toLowerCase();
            return hay.indexOf(state.search) >= 0;
        });
        if (!rows.length) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">'
                + (state.rows.length ? 'No audits match the filter.' : 'No audits are assigned to you.') + '</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        body.innerHTML = rows.map(function (x) {
            const r = x.r;
            const st    = v(r, 'auditState', 'AuditState') || '';
            const from  = onlyDate(v(r, 'scheduledFrom', 'ScheduledFrom'));
            const to    = onlyDate(v(r, 'scheduledTo', 'ScheduledTo'));
            const exec  = v(r, 'executionCode', 'ExecutionCode') || '';
            const total = v(r, 'totalEntityCount', 'TotalEntityCount');
            const scope = st === 'ScopeLive' ? 'Live'
                        : (v(r, 'scopeFrozenAt', 'ScopeFrozenAt') ? 'Frozen, ' + (total ?? 0) + ' item(s)' : '');
            return '<tr data-key="' + x.i + '">'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(r, 'engagementName', 'EngagementName') || '')
                 + ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">(' + wf.escape(v(r, 'engagementCode', 'EngagementCode') || '') + ')</span>'
                 + '<div style="color:var(--fg-subtle); font-size:12px;">' + wf.escape(v(r, 'planName', 'PlanName') || '') + '</div></td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(r, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || '')
                 + ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">(' + wf.escape(v(r, 'definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode') || '') + ')</span></td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(r, 'branchName', 'BranchName') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(from + (to ? ' - ' + to : '')) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.badge(STATE_LABEL[st] || st)
                 + (exec ? ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">' + wf.escape(exec) + '</span>' : '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(scope) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + trigger(x.i) + '</td>'
                 + '</tr>';
        }).join('');
        mountFrame();   // an open scope stays open under its row
    }

    function keyOf(row) {
        for (const k in state.byKey) if (state.byKey[k] === row) return k;
        return null;
    }

    function buildMenu(row) {
        const st = v(row, 'auditState', 'AuditState');
        const items = [];
        if (st === 'ScopeLive')
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-lock', label: 'Review & Freeze Scope', action: function () { openScope(row, false); } });
        // An id is tested against null, never for truthiness: 0 is an id
        // (557 renumbers the rows that got it, but the page must not hide
        // an audit's actions over it).
        const hasExec = v(row, 'executionId', 'ExecutionId') != null;
        if ((st === 'InProgress' || st === 'Done') && hasExec)
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-eye', label: 'View Scope', action: function () { openScope(row, true); } });
        // 567: the questions are tested in Workpapers (working papers
        // replace the 558 answers) -- In Progress to work, Done to read.
        if ((st === 'InProgress' || st === 'Done') && hasExec)
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-file-pen', label: 'Working Papers', action: function () { openWorkpapers(row); } });
        // 556: Continuous Assurance over the live or frozen scope.
        if ((st === 'ScopeLive' || st === 'InProgress' || st === 'Done') && hasExec)
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-shield-halved', label: 'Continuous Assurance', action: function () { openCa(row); } });
        if (st === 'Ready')
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-play', label: 'Start now', action: function () { load(true); } });
        return items;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Scope dialog
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function openScope(row, frozen) {
        closeScope();
        state.scope = { row: row, key: keyOf(row), items: [], frozen: frozen };
        showPane('scope');
        const branch = v(row, 'branchName', 'BranchName');
        document.getElementById('oaMyFrameCaption').textContent = frozen
            ? 'The frozen scope of this audit' + (branch ? ' at ' + branch : '') + ', with what was excluded and why.'
            : 'The audit\'s scope as it is now' + (branch ? ', narrowed to ' + branch : '')
              + '. Untick what does not apply and give the reason. Freezing is final and starts the audit.';
        document.getElementById('oaMyFrameHint').textContent = '';
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeKeepHead').hidden   = frozen;
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze').hidden     = frozen;
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeReasonHead').textContent = frozen ? 'Excluded because' : 'Reason for excluding';
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeSummary').innerHTML = '';
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeBody').innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="6" class="pm-empty">'
            + (frozen ? 'Loading the scope...' : 'Resolving the scope...') + '</td></tr>';
        document.getElementById('oaMyReview').hidden = true;   // 563: shown once loaded
        wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', '');
        mountFrame();

        const org = v(row, 'organizationId', 'OrganizationId');
        const id  = v(row, 'executionId', 'ExecutionId');
        try {
            // 563: the review (discovery / snapshot) loads beside the scope.
            const reviewP = loadReview(org, id);
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/executions/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/live-scope?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(org)),
                                  { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            state.scope.items = (j && (j.data || j.Data)) || [];
            state.scope.review = await reviewP;
            if (state.scope.row !== row) return;   // closed or switched meanwhile
            let excl = [];
            if (frozen) {
                const rx = await fetch(U(API + '/executions/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/scope-exclusions?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(org)),
                                       { credentials: 'same-origin' });
                const jx = await safeJson(rx);
                excl = rx.ok ? ((jx && (jx.data || jx.Data)) || []) : [];
            }
            renderScope(excl);
            renderReview();
        } catch (err) {
            document.getElementById('oaMyScopeBody').innerHTML = '';
            wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'The scope could not be loaded: ' + (err.message || err), 'error');
        }
    }

    function renderScope(exclusions) {
        const frozen = state.scope.frozen;
        const items  = state.scope.items;
        const counts = {};
        items.forEach(function (it) {
            const n = v(it, 'dimensionName', 'DimensionName') || v(it, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') || '';
            counts[n] = (counts[n] || 0) + 1;
        });
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeSummary').innerHTML = Object.keys(counts).map(function (k) {
            return '<span class="pm-badge">' + wf.escape(k) + ' ' + counts[k] + '</span>';
        }).join(' ') + (exclusions.length ? ' <span class="pm-badge">Excluded ' + exclusions.length + '</span>' : '');

        const keepCell = function (i) {
            return frozen ? '' : '<td><input type="checkbox" data-keep="' + i + '" checked aria-label="Keep in scope"></td>';
        };
        const rows = items.map(function (it, i) {
            return '<tr>' + keepCell(i)
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(it, 'dimensionName', 'DimensionName') || v(it, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(it, 'entityCode', 'EntityCode') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(it, 'entityName', 'EntityName') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td class="qs-cell-text">' + wf.escape(whyInScope(it)) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + (frozen ? '' : '<input class="pm-input" type="text" maxlength="1000" data-reason="' + i
                      + '" placeholder="Why it does not apply" hidden style="min-width:0; width:100%;">') + '</td>'
                 + '</tr>';
        });
        // A frozen scope also lists what was excluded, with the reason.
        exclusions.forEach(function (x) {
            rows.push('<tr style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape((v(x, 'dimensionName', 'DimensionName') || v(x, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') || '') + ' (excluded)') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(x, 'entityCode', 'EntityCode') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(x, 'entityName', 'EntityName') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td></td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(v(x, 'reason', 'Reason') || '') + '</td>'
                 + '</tr>');
        });
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeBody').innerHTML = rows.length ? rows.join('')
            : '<tr><td colspan="6" class="pm-empty">' + (frozen ? 'Nothing in scope.'
              : 'Nothing is in scope now. Check the audit\'s scope and the engagement\'s branch.') + '</td></tr>';
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze').disabled = !items.length;
        updateHint();
    }

    function updateHint() {
        if (state.scope.frozen) return;
        const out = document.querySelectorAll('#oaMyScopeBody [data-keep]:not(:checked)').length;
        const all = state.scope.items.length;
        const rv = reviewLive() ? state.scope.review : null;   // 563
        const rOut = rv ? Object.keys(rv.unkept).length : 0;
        const rMan = rv ? rv.manual.length : 0;
        document.getElementById('oaMyFrameHint').textContent =
            (all - out) + ' of ' + all + ' item(s) kept' + (out ? ', ' + out + ' excluded' : '')
            + (rOut ? '; ' + rOut + ' related record(s) unticked' : '')
            + (rMan ? '; ' + rMan + ' manual item(s)' : '');
    }

    function onKeepChange(e) {
        const cb = e.target.closest('[data-keep]');
        if (!cb) return;
        const reason = document.querySelector('[data-reason="' + cb.getAttribute('data-keep') + '"]');
        if (reason) { reason.hidden = cb.checked; if (!cb.checked) reason.focus(); }
        updateHint();
    }

    async function freeze() {
        const row = state.scope.row;
        if (!row) return;
        const excl = [];
        let missing = false;
        document.querySelectorAll('#oaMyScopeBody [data-keep]').forEach(function (cb) {
            if (cb.checked) return;
            const i  = Number(cb.getAttribute('data-keep'));
            const it = state.scope.items[i];
            const reason = (document.querySelector('[data-reason="' + i + '"]').value || '').trim();
            if (!reason) missing = true;
            excl.push({ dimensionCode: v(it, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode'), entityId: v(it, 'entityId', 'EntityId'), reason: reason });
        });
        if (missing) { wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'Give the reason for every item you exclude.', 'error'); return; }
        const keep = state.scope.items.length - excl.length;
        if (keep <= 0) { wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'Keep at least one item in scope.', 'error'); return; }
        // 563: Step 3 -- the review goes with the exclusions.
        const review = reviewPayload();
        if (review && review.missing) {
            wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'Give the reason for every related record you untick.', 'error'); return;
        }
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm('Freeze the scope with ' + keep + ' item(s)' + (excl.length ? ', ' + excl.length + ' excluded' : '')
                + '? This is final and starts the audit.', { type: 'confirm', title: 'Freeze Scope', confirmText: 'Freeze' })) return;

        const btn = document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze');
        btn.disabled = true;
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/executions/' + encodeURIComponent(v(row, 'executionId', 'ExecutionId')) + '/freeze-scope'), {
                method: 'POST', credentials: 'same-origin',
                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body: JSON.stringify({ organizationId: Number(v(row, 'organizationId', 'OrganizationId')), exclusions: excl, actor: null,
                                       review: review ? review.body : null })
            });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) { wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', (j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status), 'error'); btn.disabled = false; return; }
            closeScope();
            const rvNo = j.reviewVersionNo ?? j.ReviewVersionNo;
            wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', 'Scope frozen: ' + (j.executionCode || j.ExecutionCode || '') + ', '
                + (j.totalEntityCount ?? j.TotalEntityCount ?? keep) + ' item(s)'
                + (rvNo != null ? '; approved scope version ' + rvNo : '') + '. The audit is in progress.', 'ok');
            load(false);
        } catch (err) {
            wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', err.message || String(err), 'error');
            btn.disabled = false;
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 563: Scope Builder Step 3 -- Review and Confirm. The related records
    // of the engagement's scope (Step 2's discovery over its instances),
    // in Step 2's category list. Live: Include per category, untick a
    // record with a reason, add manual items; Freeze sends it. Frozen: the
    // approved snapshot, read-only. Practice Instances are the scope list
    // above, so they are not repeated here -- they give its "Why in scope".
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const SCOPE_CATEGORY = 'PRACTICE_INSTANCE';
    const MANUAL_CATEGORY = 'MANUAL';

    async function loadReview(org, id) {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/executions/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/scope-review?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(org)),
                                  { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            const header = (j && (j.header || j.Header)) || {};
            return {
                header     : header,
                categories : (j && (j.categories || j.Categories)) || [],
                items      : (j && (j.items || j.Items)) || [],
                open       : null,
                search     : '',
                unkept     : {},    // 'CAT|recordId' -> reason (live)
                manual     : []     // [{ categoryCode, name, note }] (live)
            };
        } catch (err) {
            // The review is an addition: without it (563 not deployed, or
            // discovery failed) the scope list still freezes as before.
            console.warn('[my-audits] scope review not available:', err);
            return null;
        }
    }

    function whyInScope(it) {
        const rv = state.scope.review;
        if (!rv || v(it, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') !== SCOPE_CATEGORY) return '';
        const id = v(it, 'entityId', 'EntityId');
        const hit = rv.items.find(function (x) {
            return v(x, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode') === SCOPE_CATEGORY && String(v(x, 'recordId', 'RecordId')) === String(id);
        });
        return hit ? (v(hit, 'reason', 'Reason') || '') : '';
    }

    function reviewLive() {
        const rv = state.scope.review;
        return !!rv && !state.scope.frozen && !v(rv.header, 'isFrozen', 'IsFrozen');
    }

    function reviewCategories() {
        const rv = state.scope.review;
        return rv ? rv.categories.filter(function (c) { return v(c, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode') !== SCOPE_CATEGORY; }) : [];
    }

    function reviewRecords(code) {
        const rv = state.scope.review;
        const q  = rv.search;
        const rows = rv.items.filter(function (x) { return v(x, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode') === code; })
            .map(function (x) {
                return { code: v(x, 'recordCode', 'RecordCode') || '', name: v(x, 'recordName', 'RecordName') || '',
                         status: v(x, 'status', 'Status') || '', reason: v(x, 'reason', 'Reason') || '',
                         id: v(x, 'recordId', 'RecordId'), kept: !!v(x, 'isKept', 'IsKept'),
                         exclusion: v(x, 'exclusionReason', 'ExclusionReason') || '',
                         manual: !!v(x, 'isManual', 'IsManual'), note: v(x, 'manualNote', 'ManualNote') || '' };
            })
            .concat(rv.manual.map(function (m, i) {
                return m.categoryCode === code
                    ? { code: '', name: m.name, status: '', reason: 'Added by the auditor', id: null, kept: true,
                        exclusion: '', manual: true, note: m.note, newIndex: i }
                    : null;
            }).filter(Boolean));
        if (!q) return rows;
        return rows.filter(function (r) {
            return [r.code, r.name, r.status, r.reason, r.note].join(' ').toLowerCase().indexOf(q) >= 0;
        });
    }

    function renderReview() {
        const rv   = state.scope.review;
        const host = document.getElementById('oaMyReview');
        if (!rv) { host.hidden = true; return; }
        host.hidden = false;
        const live = reviewLive();
        const h    = rv.header || {};
        const ver  = v(h, 'versionNo', 'VersionNo');
        const by   = v(h, 'approvedBy', 'ApprovedBy');
        const dt   = onlyDate(v(h, 'approvedDt', 'ApprovedDt'));
        document.getElementById('oaMyReviewHint').textContent = live
            ? 'What this engagement\'s scope leads to in GRAC, and why. Untick a category or a record that does not apply '
              + '(a record needs the reason), add manual items, then freeze: the result is kept as the approved scope.'
            : (ver != null
                ? 'The approved scope, version ' + ver + (by ? ', approved by ' + by : '') + (dt ? ' on ' + dt : '') + '. Read-only.'
                : 'No review was recorded for this scope: it was frozen before the review step.');
        document.getElementById('oaMyReviewSearch').value = rv.search;
        const cats = reviewCategories();
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyReviewBody');
        if (!live && ver == null) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="4" class="pm-empty">Nothing to show.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        body.innerHTML = cats.map(function (c) {
            const code  = v(c, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode');
            const name  = v(c, 'categoryName', 'CategoryName') || code;
            const inc   = !!v(c, 'isIncluded', 'IsIncluded');
            const all   = rv.items.filter(function (x) { return v(x, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode') === code; }).length
                        + rv.manual.filter(function (m) { return m.categoryCode === code; }).length;
            const shown = rv.search ? reviewRecords(code).length : all;
            const open  = rv.open === code;
            return '<tr data-rcat="' + wf.escape(code) + '"' + (open ? ' class="oa-pl-open is-selected"' : '') + ' style="cursor:pointer;">'
                 + '<td><input type="checkbox" data-rinclude="' + wf.escape(code) + '"' + (inc ? ' checked' : '')
                 +      (live ? '' : ' disabled') + ' aria-label="Include ' + wf.escape(name) + '" /></td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(name) + (inc ? '' : ' <span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">(not included)</span>') + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:right;">' + (rv.search ? shown + ' of ' + all : all) + '</td>'
                 + '<td style="text-align:center;"><i class="fa-solid ' + (open ? 'fa-chevron-up' : 'fa-chevron-down') + '" aria-hidden="true"></i></td>'
                 + '</tr>'
                 + (open ? reviewChildRow(code, inc, live) : '');
        }).join('') || '<tr><td colspan="4" class="pm-empty">Nothing related was found.</td></tr>';
    }

    // The Audit Plans child row, as Step 2: tr.oa-pl-items-row > td > .oa-pl-items.
    function reviewChildRow(code, included, live) {
        const rv   = state.scope.review;
        const rows = reviewRecords(code);
        const editable = live && included;
        const head = '<tr>' + (live ? '<th style="width:60px;">Keep</th>' : '')
                   + '<th>Code</th><th>Name</th><th>Status</th><th>Why it is related</th>'
                   + '<th>' + (live ? 'Reason for excluding / note' : 'Excluded because / note') + '</th>'
                   + (live ? '<th style="width:50px;"></th>' : '') + '</tr>';
        const lines = rows.map(function (r) {
            const key = code + '|' + r.id;
            const unkept = !r.manual && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(rv.unkept, key);
            const kept = live ? !unkept : r.kept;
            const keepCell = live
                ? '<td>' + (r.manual ? '' : '<input type="checkbox" data-rkeep="' + wf.escape(key) + '"' + (kept ? ' checked' : '')
                       + (editable ? '' : ' disabled') + ' aria-label="Keep">') + '</td>'
                : '';
            const last = r.manual
                ? '<td class="qs-cell-text">' + wf.escape(r.note) + '</td>'
                : (live
                    ? '<td>' + (unkept ? '<input class="pm-input" type="text" maxlength="1000" data-rreason="' + wf.escape(key)
                        + '" value="' + wf.escape(rv.unkept[key]) + '" placeholder="Why it does not apply" style="min-width:0; width:100%;">' : '') + '</td>'
                    : '<td class="qs-cell-text">' + wf.escape(kept ? '' : r.exclusion) + '</td>');
            const del = live
                ? '<td>' + (r.manual && r.newIndex != null
                    ? '<button type="button" class="pm-button icon" data-rdel="' + r.newIndex + '" title="Remove"><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>'
                    : '') + '</td>'
                : '';
            return '<tr' + (kept ? '' : ' style="color:var(--fg-subtle);"') + '>' + keepCell
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(r.code) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(r.name) + (r.manual ? ' ' + wf.badge('Manual') : '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + wf.escape(r.status) + '</td>'
                 + '<td class="qs-cell-text">' + wf.escape(r.reason) + '</td>'
                 + last + del + '</tr>';
        }).join('');
        const cols = live ? 7 : 5;
        const add = editable
            ? '<tr><td colspan="' + (cols - 4) + '"></td>'
              + '<td colspan="2"><input class="pm-input" type="text" maxlength="400" data-rnew-name="' + wf.escape(code)
              + '" placeholder="Manual item" style="min-width:0; width:100%;"></td>'
              + '<td><input class="pm-input" type="text" maxlength="1000" data-rnew-note="' + wf.escape(code)
              + '" placeholder="Note" style="min-width:0; width:100%;"></td>'
              + '<td><button type="button" class="pm-button" data-radd="' + wf.escape(code) + '">Add</button></td></tr>'
            : '';
        const inner = (rows.length || add)
            ? '<div class="pm-table-wrap"><table><thead>' + head + '</thead><tbody>'
              + (lines || '<tr><td colspan="' + cols + '" class="pm-empty">' + (rv.search ? 'No records match the search.' : 'No related records.') + '</td></tr>')
              + add + '</tbody></table></div>'
            : '<div class="pm-empty" style="padding:8px 0;">' + (rv.search ? 'No records match the search.' : 'No related records.') + '</div>';
        return '<tr class="oa-pl-items-row is-selected"><td colspan="4"><div class="oa-pl-items">' + inner + '</div></td></tr>';
    }

    function wireReview() {
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyReviewBody');
        document.getElementById('oaMyReviewSearch').addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            if (!state.scope.review) return;
            state.scope.review.search = e.target.value.trim().toLowerCase();
            renderReview();
            const box = document.getElementById('oaMyReviewSearch');
            box.focus();
            box.setSelectionRange(box.value.length, box.value.length);
        });
        body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            const rv = state.scope.review;
            if (!rv) return;
            const add = e.target.closest('[data-radd]');
            if (add) {
                const code = add.getAttribute('data-radd');
                const nameEl = body.querySelector('[data-rnew-name="' + code + '"]');
                const noteEl = body.querySelector('[data-rnew-note="' + code + '"]');
                const name = (nameEl && nameEl.value || '').trim();
                if (!name) { wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'Give the manual item a name.', 'error'); if (nameEl) nameEl.focus(); return; }
                rv.manual.push({ categoryCode: code, name: name, note: (noteEl && noteEl.value || '').trim() });
                wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', '');
                renderReview();
                updateHint();
                return;
            }
            const del = e.target.closest('[data-rdel]');
            if (del) {
                rv.manual.splice(Number(del.getAttribute('data-rdel')), 1);
                renderReview();
                updateHint();
                return;
            }
            if (e.target.closest('input, button')) return;
            const tr = e.target.closest('tr[data-rcat]');
            if (!tr) return;
            const code = tr.getAttribute('data-rcat');
            rv.open = rv.open === code ? null : code;
            renderReview();
        });
        body.addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            const rv = state.scope.review;
            if (!rv || !reviewLive()) return;
            const inc = e.target.closest('[data-rinclude]');
            if (inc) {
                const code = inc.getAttribute('data-rinclude');
                rv.categories.forEach(function (c) {
                    if (v(c, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode') === code) { c.isIncluded = inc.checked; c.IsIncluded = inc.checked; }
                });
                renderReview();
                updateHint();
                return;
            }
            const keep = e.target.closest('[data-rkeep]');
            if (keep) {
                const key = keep.getAttribute('data-rkeep');
                if (keep.checked) delete rv.unkept[key]; else rv.unkept[key] = '';
                renderReview();
                if (!keep.checked) {
                    const box = body.querySelector('[data-rreason="' + key + '"]');
                    if (box) box.focus();
                }
                updateHint();
            }
        });
        body.addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            const rv = state.scope.review;
            const box = e.target.closest('[data-rreason]');
            if (rv && box) rv.unkept[box.getAttribute('data-rreason')] = box.value;
        });
    }

    // { body: { categories, excluded, manual }, missing } -- null without a review.
    function reviewPayload() {
        const rv = state.scope.review;
        if (!reviewLive()) return null;
        let missing = false;
        const excluded = Object.keys(rv.unkept).map(function (key) {
            const at = key.indexOf('|');
            const reason = (rv.unkept[key] || '').trim();
            if (!reason) missing = true;
            return { categoryCode: key.slice(0, at), recordId: Number(key.slice(at + 1)), reason: reason };
        });
        return {
            missing: missing,
            body: {
                categories: rv.categories.map(function (c) {
                    return { code: v(c, 'categoryCode', 'CategoryCode'), isIncluded: !!v(c, 'isIncluded', 'IsIncluded') };
                }),
                excluded: excluded,
                manual: rv.manual.map(function (m) { return { categoryCode: m.categoryCode, name: m.name, note: m.note || null }; })
            }
        };
    }

    // The frame in a row under the audit's row (Audit Configuration's
    // mountFrame / unmountStep, 543). Called again after the list is
    // re-rendered, so an open scope stays open.
    function mountFrame() {
        const key = state.scope.key;
        if (key == null) return;
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyBody');
        const old = body.querySelector('tr.oa-pl-items-row');
        if (old) old.remove();
        const row  = body.querySelector('tr[data-key="' + key + '"]');
        // the audit is filtered out of the list: the frame goes back to its
        // holder and closes (it is held by reference, never looked up by id,
        // because re-rendering the list takes it out of the page)
        if (!row) { closeScope(); return; }
        // The Audit Plans child row: tr.oa-pl-items-row > td > .oa-pl-items.
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.className = 'oa-pl-items-row is-selected';
        const td = document.createElement('td');
        td.colSpan = 7;
        const host = document.createElement('div');
        host.className = 'oa-pl-items';
        host.appendChild(myFrame());
        td.appendChild(host);
        tr.appendChild(td);
        row.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', tr);
        row.classList.add('oa-pl-open', 'is-selected');
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 556: Continuous Assurance -- the same frame, read-only.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function showPane(which) {
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopePane').hidden = which !== 'scope';
        document.getElementById('oaMyCaPane').hidden    = which !== 'ca';
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 567: Working Papers -- the Workpapers page on this execution; the
    // execution travels in the navigation code (never in the address).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function openWorkpapers(row) {
        const err = await window.gracSecureNav.open('org-my-audits', 'org-workpapers', 'AssuranceExecution',
            v(row, 'executionId', 'ExecutionId'), v(row, 'organizationId', 'OrganizationId'),
            v(row, 'executionCode', 'ExecutionCode'));
        if (err) wf.setMessage('oaMyMessage', err, 'error');
    }

    async function openCa(row) {
        closeScope();
        state.scope = { row: row, key: keyOf(row), items: [], frozen: true };
        showPane('ca');
        const live   = v(row, 'auditState', 'AuditState') === 'ScopeLive';
        const branch = v(row, 'branchName', 'BranchName');
        document.getElementById('oaMyFrameCaption').textContent =
            'Continuous Assurance over the ' + (live ? 'live' : 'frozen') + ' scope' + (branch ? ' at ' + branch : '')
            + ': each scope item, the practice instances it covers, their scheduled obligations, the obligation status and the last task.';
        document.getElementById('oaMyFrameHint').textContent = 'Read-only. Each obligation is counted once in the summary.';
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze').hidden = true;
        document.getElementById('oaMyCaSummary').innerHTML = '';
        document.getElementById('oaMyCaBody').innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="5" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', '');
        mountFrame();

        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/executions/' + encodeURIComponent(v(row, 'executionId', 'ExecutionId'))
                    + '/continuous-assurance?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(v(row, 'organizationId', 'OrganizationId'))),
                    { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const j = await safeJson(r);
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            renderCa((j && (j.summary || j.Summary)) || [], (j && (j.detail || j.Detail)) || []);
        } catch (err) {
            document.getElementById('oaMyCaBody').innerHTML = '';
            wf.setMessage('oaMyScopeMessage', 'Continuous Assurance could not be loaded: ' + (err.message || err), 'error');
        }
    }

    function renderCa(summary, detail) {
        const group = function (kind, title) {
            const rows = summary.filter(function (x) { return v(x, 'summaryKind', 'SummaryKind') === kind; });
            if (!rows.length) return '';
            return '<div style="margin-bottom:6px;"><span style="color:var(--fg-muted); font-size:12px; margin-right:6px;">' + wf.escape(title) + '</span>'
                 + rows.map(function (x) {
                       return '<span class="pm-badge">' + wf.escape(v(x, 'label', 'Label') || '') + ' ' + wf.escape(String(v(x, 'itemCount', 'ItemCount') ?? 0)) + '</span>';
                   }).join(' ') + '</div>';
        };
        document.getElementById('oaMyCaSummary').innerHTML =
            group('Totals', 'Totals') + group('ObligationStatus', 'Obligation status') + group('LastTaskStatus', 'Last task');

        if (!detail.length) {
            document.getElementById('oaMyCaBody').innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="5" class="pm-empty">Nothing is in scope.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        const muted = function (t) { return '<span style="color:var(--fg-subtle);">' + wf.escape(t) + '</span>'; };
        let lastItem = null, lastInst = null;
        document.getElementById('oaMyCaBody').innerHTML = detail.map(function (d) {
            const itemKey = (v(d, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') || '') + ':' + (v(d, 'entityId', 'EntityId') ?? '');
            const instId  = v(d, 'practiceInstanceId', 'PracticeInstanceId');
            const firstOfItem = itemKey !== lastItem;
            const firstOfInst = firstOfItem || String(instId) !== String(lastInst);
            lastItem = itemKey; lastInst = instId;

            const item = firstOfItem
                ? wf.escape(v(d, 'entityName', 'EntityName') || v(d, 'entityCode', 'EntityCode') || '')
                  + '<div style="color:var(--fg-subtle); font-size:12px;">' + wf.escape(v(d, 'dimensionName', 'DimensionName') || v(d, 'dimensionCode', 'DimensionCode') || '') + '</div>'
                : '';
            let inst = '';
            if (instId == null) inst = firstOfItem ? muted('No practice instance covers this item') : '';
            else if (firstOfInst)
                inst = wf.escape(v(d, 'instanceName', 'InstanceName') || '')
                     + ' ' + muted('(' + (v(d, 'instanceCode', 'InstanceCode') || '') + ')')
                     + '<div style="color:var(--fg-subtle); font-size:12px;">' + wf.escape(v(d, 'via', 'Via') || '') + '</div>';

            const obId = v(d, 'obligationId', 'ObligationId');
            const ob = obId == null
                ? (instId == null ? '' : muted('No scheduled obligation'))
                : wf.escape(v(d, 'obligationName', 'ObligationName') || '')
                  + '<div style="color:var(--fg-subtle); font-size:12px;">' + wf.escape([v(d, 'obligationType', 'ObligationType'), v(d, 'frequency', 'Frequency')].filter(Boolean).join(' - ')) + '</div>';
            const st = obId == null ? '' : wf.badge(v(d, 'obligationStatusName', 'ObligationStatusName') || 'Not set');
            const tn = v(d, 'lastTaskNumber', 'LastTaskNumber');
            const task = obId == null ? '' : (tn
                ? wf.escape(tn) + ' ' + wf.badge(v(d, 'lastTaskStatusName', 'LastTaskStatusName') || '')
                  + '<div style="color:var(--fg-subtle); font-size:12px;">Due ' + wf.escape(onlyDate(v(d, 'lastTaskDueDate', 'LastTaskDueDate'))) + '</div>'
                : muted('No task yet'));
            return '<tr><td>' + item + '</td><td>' + inst + '</td><td>' + ob + '</td><td>' + st + '</td><td>' + task + '</td></tr>';
        }).join('');
    }

    let myFrameEl = null;
    function myFrame() { return myFrameEl || (myFrameEl = document.getElementById('oaMyFrame')); }
    function closeScope() {
        document.getElementById('oaMyHolder').appendChild(myFrame());
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyBody');
        const tr = body.querySelector('tr.oa-pl-items-row');
        if (tr) tr.remove();
        body.querySelectorAll('tr.oa-pl-open').forEach(function (r) { r.classList.remove('oa-pl-open', 'is-selected'); });
        state.scope = { row: null, key: null, items: [], frozen: false, review: null };
        document.getElementById('oaMyScopeFreeze').disabled = false;
        document.getElementById('oaMyReview').hidden = true;   // 563
        showPane('scope');
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Row menu -- the Audit Plans page's pattern (portal to body).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function trigger(key) {
        return '<button type="button" class="pm-action-trigger"'
             + ' data-key="' + key + '"'
             + ' aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" title="Actions">'
             + '<i class="fas fa-ellipsis-v fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical" aria-hidden="true"></i>'
             + '<span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span>'
             + '</button>';
    }
    function closeRowMenu() {
        if (openMenuEl) { openMenuEl.remove(); openMenuEl = null; }
        if (openMenuTrigger) { openMenuTrigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'); openMenuTrigger = null; }
    }
    function positionRowMenu(trg) {
        if (!openMenuEl) return;
        const r  = trg.getBoundingClientRect();
        const mr = openMenuEl.getBoundingClientRect();
        const gap = 6;
        let top = r.bottom + gap, left = r.right - mr.width;
        if (top + mr.height > window.innerHeight - 8) top = Math.max(8, r.top - mr.height - gap);
        if (left < 8) left = 8;
        if (left + mr.width > window.innerWidth - 8) left = window.innerWidth - mr.width - 8;
        openMenuEl.style.top  = top  + 'px';
        openMenuEl.style.left = left + 'px';
    }
    function openRowMenu(trg, items) {
        closeRowMenu();
        openMenuTrigger = trg;
        trg.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        openMenuEl = document.createElement('div');
        openMenuEl.className = 'pm-action-menu';
        openMenuEl.setAttribute('role', 'menu');
        if (!items.length) {
            const p = document.createElement('div');
            p.style.cssText = 'padding:8px 12px; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-subtle); white-space:nowrap;';
            p.textContent = 'No actions available';
            openMenuEl.appendChild(p);
        }
        for (const it of items) {
            const b = document.createElement('button');
            b.type = 'button'; b.setAttribute('role', 'menuitem');
            b.innerHTML = '<i class="fa-solid ' + wf.escape(it.icon) + '" aria-hidden="true"></i> ' + wf.escape(it.label);
            b.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                closeRowMenu();
                try { it.action(); } catch (err) { console.error('[my-audits] menu action failed', err); }
            });
            openMenuEl.appendChild(b);
        }
        document.body.appendChild(openMenuEl);
        positionRowMenu(trg);
    }
    function wireRowMenus() {
        const body = document.getElementById('oaMyBody');
        body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            const trg = e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger');
            if (!trg || !body.contains(trg)) return;
            e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
            if (openMenuTrigger === trg) { closeRowMenu(); return; }
            const row = state.byKey[trg.getAttribute('data-key')];
            if (row) openRowMenu(trg, buildMenu(row));
        });
        document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            if (!openMenuEl) return;
            if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-menu'))    return;
            if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger')) return;
            closeRowMenu();
        });
        document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { if (e.key === 'Escape') closeRowMenu(); });
        window.addEventListener('resize', closeRowMenu);
        window.addEventListener('scroll',  closeRowMenu, true);
    }

    function onlyDate(val) {
        if (!val) return '';
        if (typeof window.gracFormatDisplayDate === "function") { var g = window.gracFormatDisplayDate(val); if (g !== val) return g; }
        return String(val).slice(0, 10);
    }
    async function safeJson(r) { try { return await r.json(); } catch (_) { return null; } }
})();
</script>
